ADDENDUM (written 19:3x, after t_count ran and BEFORE t_count2 runs; PREDICTIONS.txt itself is never amended):
t_count measured something other than it was built for: the gate's own `unknown=` line does arithmetic on `bare`, so
under `set -u` BOTH derivers stop at eval with "x: unbound variable", rc 1 -- fail-closed, but F6's count check is never
reached.  A mis-built control, recorded as such.  A NEW case, predicted here first:
  t_count2  the scratch gate's `conv_mark=` line replaced by `conv_mark=$(echo x)`: the report
              F6 DERIVE_FAIL rc 3 (the census value conv_mark is [x])      F5 rc 0, a report printing x as the fresh-mark count
